WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:04.334
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.701
You're here.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.501
Look at this place. It's crazy.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.100
Guys, it's the holiday season.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.868
And for the first time
in three years,

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.234
office holiday parties are back.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:20.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.901
Yep, it's that magical night
when you say,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.067
"let's not talk about work"
and then only talk about work.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.601
Yeah, it's the same
conversations you have at work,

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:28.834
but now they're an inch
from your ear

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.167
and 10 times the volume.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.067
-[ Loud music plays ]
-"I'm thinking about following

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.834
up with Brian about that raise!"

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:36.968
[ Music stops ]

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:39.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:42.334
That's right. The party is
basically this meme,

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.767
plus Santa hats.

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.367
Yep, every office holiday party
is the same.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.968
They all start
with a champagne toast

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.367
and end with half the staff
updating their LinkedIn.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.400
I love the holiday season.
I love Christmas music.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.501
Of course, everyone has a
favorite Christmas song.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.067
Quest, we all know
what yours is.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:03.167
-Wait, wha-- wha-- what? What?
-Oh, come on.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.834
♪ Come they told me,
pa-rum-pa-pum-pum ♪

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.801
-[ Laughter ]
-That's not my favorite song.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.334
-Of course it is. You're a --
You're a drummer.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.701
♪ A newborn king to see,
pa-rum-pa-pum-pum ♪

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.334
-Ah.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:17.100
No. No, it's not. Seriously.
It's not.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.200
-♪ Our finest gifts we bring,
pa-rum-pa-pum-pum ♪

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.100
[ Drums playing ]

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.434
-♪ To lay before the king,
pa-rum-pa-pum-pum ♪

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.033
♪ Rum-pa-pum-pum,
rum-pa-pum-pum ♪

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:31.234
[ Drum solo ]

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:35.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.534
-Uh, Jimmy, my favorite song

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:39.634
is still "Jingle Bells."

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.501
-[ Laughter ]
-Oh. Maybe I was wrong.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:43.868
Let's get to some news.

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:46.334
The White House chief of staff
said that he expects

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:49.234
President Biden to announce that
he's running for re-election

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.834
after the holidays.

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.200
That makes sense.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.868
Most Americans announce
they're going to start running

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.067
after the holidays.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.868
Also, I'm no political expert,
but if you announce that

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.334
you're going to make
an announcement,

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:02.801
isn't that the announcement?

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.434
Speaking of running for
president, new polling shows

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.467
that in a potential 2024
matchup, Biden is tied with

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.234
Florida governor Ron DeSantis,

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.767
while DeSantis leads former
president Trump by 10 points.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.868
-Ooh.
-Yep, Biden, DeSantis,

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.334
and Trump -- it's like your
grandfather, your crazy uncle,

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:21.267
and the family member
nobody talks about anymore.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:24.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:28.501
Yep, Trump's unfavorable rating
has surged to 67%.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.734
To give you an idea of how bad
that is, Kanye is only at 66.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:32.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:35.067
Bad.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.467
Some more 2024 news --former
Trump national security adviser

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:39.767
John Bolton said that

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.400
he's considering running
for president.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.868
He's even been testing out
some campaign slogans

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.267
to see what people respond to.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.467
Check these out.
First there's...

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:55.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.300
Then there's...

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:01.934
-Oh!
-[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.267
-And finally, there's...

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.534
"Anything!
You'll never get it from me."

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:14.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.534
That's right, John Bolton said
that he's considering

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.968
a 2024 presidential run
to challenge Trump.

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:20.167
Can we see Bolton?

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.834
There he is. Yeah, well, he --

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.167
He already has
a fair amount of support.

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.100
Check out what some of
his supporters are saying.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.501
First up, Geraldo Rivera said...

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.400
Then actor Sam Elliott said...

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.267
And singer David Crosby said...

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.400
Then Hulk Hogan said...

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:47.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:48.801
Then the Monopoly Man said...

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:57.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.667
And finally the Lorax said...

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:03.667
Can't help it.

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.834
Did you guys see this?
This is real.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:10.300
During a hearing, Rudy Giuliani
was caught on a hot mike telling

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.133
his lawyer that he accidentally
wore two watches.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.067
Now, the quality of the footage
is bad,

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:17.868
but it doesn't disappoint.
Check this out.

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:20.467
-So, I'm at a good place
to stop, Mr. Chair.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.033
-Thank you.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.734
You know I have two watches on?

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:32.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:33.567
-What?

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:36.067
-Just a reminder, that was
Trump's top lawyer.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:39.767
Two watches.
-Ah.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.267
-Oh, this is very cool.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.701
Researchers in Germany have
developed Golfi,

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:46.434
a golfing robot that can make
perfect putts.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.100
-Hmm.
-Yeah. And that's not all.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.801
Here's a full list of
what Golfi can do.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.868
It can, of course, play golf,

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:55.300
or it can put his hand
on your shoulder.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.200
It can say,
"I'm proud of you, son."

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.467
And it can kiss your mom.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.501
Wait, kiss your mom?

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:07.100
Yup. Now Golfi's moving in.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.467
He's calling you "champ"

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.267
and showing up to
your baseball games.

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:11.734
"Great catch, kid,
but you really

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.100
should have thrown to third."

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.767
"Shut up,
you're not my real dad."

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:17.133
"Yes, I am. Why do you think
you have robot legs?"

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.634
Look down.
Oh, God, you do have robot legs.

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.434
Robot arms, robot face.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:22.968
He's right. You're not human.

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.501
You're Golfi Jr.

00:05:24.501 --> 00:05:32.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.834
Well, here's some good news.

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.968
I saw that the head of the CDC
said the updated flu vaccine

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:40.267
looks like a very good match
for this year's strains.

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.234
Basically the vaccine saw
the strains

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:43.434
and was like, "Swipe right."

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.367
It's not a perfect match.
But like most people, the flu is

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.400
just happy to go home with
someone for the holidays.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.367
Well, guys, get this.

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:54.801
"Dahmer" just became
the third show on Netflix

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:58.067
to hit 1 billion hours
viewed in 60 days.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:05:59.968
-Wow!
-And if someone mentions that

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:02.501
at the office holiday party,
do not split an Uber home.

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:04.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:08.334
Finally, guys, we have exactly
nine shows left before we go on

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.133
Christmas break, which means
it's time for that

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:11.767
beloved "Tonight Show"
tradition.

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:16.000
It's time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters."

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.534
-♪ 12 days of
Christmas sweaters ♪

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.133
♪ Nine days left ♪

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:22.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.300
-That's right.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.801
Every show between now and
Christmas, we'll be giving

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:31.634
one lucky audience member
a superb Christmas sweater

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:33.634
from the "Countdown to
Christmas" cabinet.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:37.501
Since there are nine shows left,
let's open door number nine.

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:41.267
You feeling it?
-Yeah.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.734
-Whoo! Alright, let's see it.

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:45.334
Ooh.

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:50.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:51.834
What?

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:58.234
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:06:58.234 --> 00:07:02.567
The head -- the he-- your head
comes through the chimney?

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:03.834
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:07:03.834 --> 00:07:06.667
This is a special, special
sweater right here.

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:08.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:11.767
Wow. A lot going on.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:14.467
Now let's see who is going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:15.834
Everyone, look at
your seat number.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.534
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.100
Quest, can I get a drumroll,
please?

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.334
[ Drumroll ]

00:07:20.334 --> 00:07:21.868
Who wants this sweater?
It's a one of a kind.

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:22.801
It's a good one.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:25.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.467 --> 00:07:27.801
2-3-9.

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:29.267
♪♪

00:07:29.267 --> 00:07:32.934
Come on down. Come on down.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:40.000
♪♪

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.200
Hey!

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.167
Nice to see ya.
Stand over there.

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:48.434
How are ya?
-Good, how are you?

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.968
-I'm great. What's your name
and where are you from?

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:51.701
-I'm Sarah.
I live in New York, actually.

00:07:51.701 --> 00:07:54.334
-Yeah, it's a local New Yorker.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:54.334 --> 00:07:58.901
-Sarah, do you have anything
like this in your wardrobe?

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:00.801
-I don't.
But I'm totally wearing it.

00:08:00.801 --> 00:08:01.834
I'm totally gonna wear it.
-Yeah.

00:08:01.834 --> 00:08:03.701
Would you like
to wear it tonight?

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:05.200
-Yeah.
Oh, you want me to put it on?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.367
I'll put it on right now.
-Yeah. I'd love it. Yeah.

00:08:06.367 --> 00:08:08.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:10.567
-Be careful with it.
-How do I --

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:12.167
-I don't -- I don't know how.

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:14.734
But your head somehow comes
through the chimney hole.

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:16.567
I think you're right.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:17.767
Can you feel my hand?
-Yes.

00:08:17.767 --> 00:08:20.567
-Okay. Where --

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:23.000
No, not your hands, your head.
-No, yes.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.367
-Yeah, your hands go
through the sleeves.

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:26.501
-We got it.
-Oh, oh, wait, this is --

00:08:26.501 --> 00:08:27.801
Yeah, perfect.

00:08:27.801 --> 00:08:29.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:31.767
Oh, my God. It's perfect.

00:08:31.767 --> 00:08:33.133
Yes, it looks great.

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:34.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:38.100
[ Laughing ]

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.834
That's fantastic.

00:08:39.834 --> 00:08:41.200
Look at how good you look.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.834
It looks so --
Come on, give her a round of --

00:08:42.834 --> 00:08:44.367
Sarah from New York.

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:45.667
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:47.667
Happy holidays.
Thank you.

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:50.033
-Stick around. We'll be right
back with "WeTweet," everybody.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:51.467
Come on back to the show.

00:08:51.467 --> 00:09:00.133
♪♪

